From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:29:52 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: draw the expanded plan's scrollbar always
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wave 2 of the Zeo next proposal (docs/ZEO-NEXT-PROPOSAL.md §5.1, asks 27
and 31; finding F1). Upstream caps the expanded item plan at `max_h_40`
and scrolls it, but draws no scrollbar, so a list longer than the cap
gave no sign that it went on. Claude Agent (Plus) 0.36 sends its task
list as a keyed plan that Zed no longer prunes, so the list that stays
on screen can now outgrow the cap more often.

The list keeps its cap and now draws its scrollbar always
(`Scrollbars::always_visible`, tracked by a `ScrollHandle` on the
ThreadView) — `Scrollbars::new` hides the thumb a second after the
pointer enters, which story 034 measured.

Why the element is built in `render()`: drawing a scrollbar needs a
mutable `App`, and `render_activity_bar` holds the thread borrowed
through `&Context` for its whole body. `render_scrollable_plan_items`
builds the list where `cx` is mutable and hands it to
`render_activity_bar`, which gained a `plan_items` argument; a markdown
plan, a collapsed plan and a `None` still render exactly as before.
`render_plan_entries` returns its `Stateful<Div>` so the scroll handle
can be attached.

Verified 2026-11-09 in the prepared d2a4fb6 tree: cargo check --tests,
cargo clippy --tests and cargo fmt --check clean on agent_ui; cargo test
-p agent_ui --lib 1521 passed, the 3 that fail share the process-wide
logger and pass alone. The scrollbar itself is for an Xvfb capture: GPUI
tests do not see auto-hide.
